"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins and the absence of seminal vesicle invasion and lymph node metastasis, which are positive prognostic indicators. The surgical pathology reported a Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3) and pT3a stage with extraprostatic extension. Countervailing factors include the preoperative PSA of 6.2 and the missing Gleason pattern and ISUP report from the biopsy, which limits the assessment of the initial tumor characteristics. The nodal status was documented as no lymph node metastasis. The uncertainty in the prognosis is heightened by the missing postoperative PSA and subsequent follow-up data, which are necessary to track the trajectory of the disease. Information regarding the postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory would significantly revise this assessment. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 50.23–75.35 months; its coverage has not been validated."
